helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154348				0	gl	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> String that represents a number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	gl	Using the Val function, you can convert a string that represents numbers into numeric expressions. This is the inverse of the \<emph\>Str\</emph\> function. If only part of the string contains numbers, only the first appropriate characters of the string are converted. If the string does not contain any numbers, the \<emph\>Val\</emph\> function returns the value 0.				20200411 15:09:53
