helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153539				0	gl	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03120301.xhp\" name=\"Format Function [Runtime]\"\>Format Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3156042				0	gl	Converte un número nunha cadea e formátao de acordo co especificado.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145090				0	gl	Sintaxe:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	gl	Format (Número [, Formato As String])				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149178				0	gl	Valor de retorno:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	gl	Cadea				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159176				0	gl	Parámetros:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415				0	gl	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that you want to convert to a formatted string.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147531				0	gl	\<emph\>Format:\</emph\> String that specifies the format code for the number. If \<emph\>Format\</emph\> is omitted, the Format function works like the \<emph\>Str\</emph\> function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147561				0	gl	Códigos de formatado				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	gl	A seguinte lista describe os códigos que pode usar para formatar un número:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153380				0	gl	\<emph\>0:\</emph\> If \<emph\>Number\</emph\> has a digit at the position of the 0 in the format code, the digit is displayed, otherwise a zero is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210				0	gl	If \<emph\>Number\</emph\> has fewer digits than the number of zeros in the format code, (on either side of the decimal), leading or trailing zeros are displayed. If the number has more digits to the left of the decimal separator than the amount of zeros in the format code, the additional digits are displayed without formatting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176	14			0	gl	Decimal places in the number are rounded according to the number of zeros that appear after the decimal separator in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>code.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	gl	\<emph\>#:\</emph\> If \<emph\>Number\</emph\> contains a digit at the position of the # placeholder in the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> code, the digit is displayed, otherwise nothing is displayed at this position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148452	16			0	gl	Este símbolo funciona como o 0, excepto polo feito de que os ceros á esquerda ou á dereita non se mostran se hai máis caracteres # no código de formato que díxitos no número. Só se mostran os díxitos relevantes do número.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3159150				0	gl	\<emph\>.:\</emph\> The decimal placeholder determines the number of decimal places to the left and right of the decimal separator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3159252				0	gl	Se o código de formato contén só marcadores # á esquerda deste símbolo, os números menores que 1 comezan cun separador decimal. Para mostrar sempre un cero á esquerda dos números fraccionarios , use 0 como marcador para o primeiro díxito á esquerda do separador decimal.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368				0	gl	\<emph\>%:\</emph\> Multiplies the number by 100 and inserts the percent sign (%) where the number appears in the format code.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	gl	\<emph\>E- E+ e- e+ :\</emph\> If the format code contains at least one digit placeholder (0 or #) to the right of the symbol E-, E+, e-, or e+, the number is formatted in the scientific or exponential format. The letter E or e is inserted between the number and the exponent. The number of placeholders for digits to the right of the symbol determines the number of digits in the exponent.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	gl	Se o expoñente é negativo, o signo menos móstrase directamente antes con E-, E+, e-, e+. Se é positivo, o signo máis só se mostra antes de expoñentes con E+ ou e+.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148617				0	gl	O delimitador de millar móstrase se o código de formato contén o delimitador entre marcadores de díxito (0 ou #).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3163713				0	gl	O uso do punto como separador decimal e de millares depende da configuración rexional. Cando introduza un número directamente no código fonte de Basic, utilice sempre como separador decimal o punto. O carácter mostrado como separador decimal depende do formato de número do seu sistema.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3152887				0	gl	\<emph\>- + $ ( ) space:\</emph\> A plus (+), minus (-), dollar ($), space, or brackets entered directly in the format code is displayed as a literal character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	gl	To display characters other than the ones listed here, you must precede it by a backslash (\\), or enclose it in quotation marks (" ").				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153139				0	gl	\\ : The backslash displays the next character in the format code.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153366				0	gl	Characters in the format code that have a special meaning can only be displayed as literal characters if they are preceded by a backslash. The backslash itself is not displayed, unless you enter a double backslash (\\\\) in the format code.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411				0	gl	Os caracteres que deben precederse dunha barra invertida no código de formato para mostrarse como caracteres literais son: caracteres de formato de data e hora (a, c, d, h, m, n, p, q, s, t, w, y, /, :), caracteres de formato numérico (#, 0, %, E, e, coma, punto) e caracteres de formato de cadea de caracteres (@, &, <, >, !).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	gl	Tamén pode usar os seguintes formatos numéricos predefinidos. Excepto para "Número xeral", todos os códigos predefinidos devolven o número con dous decimais.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150113				0	gl	Se usa formatos predefinidos, o nome do formato debe situarse entre comiñas.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377				0	gl	Formato predefinido				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	gl	\<emph\>General Number:\</emph\> Numbers are displayed as entered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	gl	\<emph\>Currency:\</emph\> Inserts a dollar sign in front of the number and encloses negative numbers in brackets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	gl	\<emph\>Fixed:\</emph\> Displays at least one digit in front of the decimal separator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	gl	\<emph\>Standard:\</emph\> Displays numbers with a thousands separator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	gl	\<emph\>Percent:\</emph\> Multiplies the number by 100 and appends a percent sign to the number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153836				0	gl	\<emph\>Scientific:\</emph\> Displays numbers in scientific format (for example, 1.00E+03 for 1000).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	gl	Un código de formato pode dividirse en tres seccións separadas por punto e coma. A primeira parte define o formato para valores positivos, a segunda para valores negativos e a terceira para cero. Se só especifica un código de formato, aplícase a todos os números.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149019				0	gl	Exemplo:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3156054				0	gl	Sub ExemploFormat				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148993				0	gl	MsgBox Format(6328.2, "##,##0.00")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A2				0	gl	REM utilice sempre un punto como separador decimal ao introducir números no código fonte de Basic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339				0	gl	REM mostra por exemplo 6,328.20 no contorno local inglés, 6.328,20 no alemán.				20200411 15:09:53
