helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317				0	gl	Declaración de variábeis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150299	18			0	gl	In $[officename] Basic you don't need to declare variables explicitly. A variable declaration can be performed with the \<emph\>Dim\</emph\> statement. You can declare more than one variable at a time by separating the names with a comma. To define the variable type, use either a type-declaration sign after the name, or the appropriate key word. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154118				0	gl	Exemplos de declaracións de variábeis:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	gl	DIM a$				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982				0	gl	Declara a variábel "a" como String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149531				0	gl	DIM a As String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150343				0	gl	Declara a variábel "a" como String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149036				0	gl	DIM a$, b As Integer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155507				0	gl	Declara unha variábel como String e outra como Integer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10854				0	gl	DIM c As Boolean				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10859				0	gl	Declara c como variábel booleana que é VERDADEIRA ou FALSA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519				0	gl	Ao declarar variábeis, é moi importante que utilice sempre o carácter de declaración de tipo, mesmo que se usara na declaración en vez dunha palabra chave. Deste modo, as seguintes instrucións non son válidas:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	gl	DIM a$				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154527				0	gl	Declara "a" como String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148599				0	gl	a="TestString"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153064				0	gl	Ausencia de declaración de tipo: "a$="				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3144770				0	gl	Despois de declarar unha variábel como dun tipo específico, non pode declarala de novo co mesmo nome e un tipo diferente!				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149331				0	gl	Obrigatoriedade das declaracións de variábeis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149443				0	gl	Use a seguinte orde para forzar a declaración de variábeis:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	gl	OPTION EXPLICIT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155072				0	gl	The \<emph\>Option Explicit\</emph\> statement has to be the first line in the module, before the first SUB. Generally, only arrays need to be declared explicitly. All other variables are declared according to the type-declaration character, or - if omitted - as the default type \<emph\>Single\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154614				0	gl	Tipos de variábeis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155383				0	gl	$[officename] Basic admite catro clases de variábeis:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153972	36			0	gl	\<emph\>Numeric\</emph\> variables can contain number values. Some variables are used to store large or small numbers, and others are used for floating-point or fractional numbers. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159226				0	gl	\<emph\>String\</emph\> variables contain character strings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145217				0	gl	\<emph\>Boolean\</emph\> variables contain either the TRUE or the FALSE value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	gl	\<emph\>Object\</emph\> variables can store objects of various types, like tables and documents within a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153805				0	gl	Variábeis enteiras				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146966				0	gl	As variábeis enteiras comprenden o intervalo de -32768 a 32767. Se atribúe un valor de punto flotante a unha variábel de número enteiro, os decimais arredóndanse ao número enteiro máis próximo. As variábeis enteiras calcúlanse rapidamente nos procedementos e son apropiadas como variábeis contador en lazos. Esas variábeis só requiren dous bytes de memoria. O carácter de declaración de tipo desas variábeis é o "%".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810				0	gl	Dim Variábel%				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153556				0	gl	Variábel Dim como enteiro				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147546				0	gl	Variábeis enteiras longas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193				0	gl	As variábeis enteiras longas comprenden o intervalo -2147483648 a 2147483647. Se atribúe un valor de punto flotante a unha variábel de número enteiro longo, os decimais arredóndanse ao número enteiro máis próximo. As variábeis enteiras longas calcúlanse rapidamente nos procedementos e son apropiadas para contadores por lazos con valores maiores. Esas variábeis requiren catro bytes de memoria. O carácter de declaración de tipo desas variábeis é o "&".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154708				0	gl	Variábel& Dim				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156365				0	gl	Variábel Dim como longo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id7596972				0	gl	Decimal Variables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id2649311				0	gl	Decimal variables can take positive or negative numbers or zero. Accuracy is up to 29 digits.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id7617114				0	gl	You can use plus (+) or minus (-) signs as prefixes for decimal numbers (with or without spaces).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id1593676				0	gl	If a decimal number is assigned to an integer variable, %PRODUCTNAME Basic rounds the figure up or down.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147500				0	gl	Variábeis simples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153070				0	gl	As variábeis simples conteñen valores positivos ou negativos entre 3.402823 x 10E38 e 1.401298 x 10E-45. Son variábeis de punto flotante onde a precisión decimal diminúe cando a parte non decimal aumenta. Son apropiadas para cálculos matemáticos de precisión mediana. Os cálculos precisan de máis tempo que as variábeis enteiras aínda que son máis rápidos que con variábeis duplas. As variábeis simples requiren 4 bytes de memoria. O carácter de declaración de tipo é "!".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	gl	Variábel Dim				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153302				0	gl	Variábel Dim como simple				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155753				0	gl	Variábeis duplas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150953				0	gl	As variábeis duplas conteñen valores positivos ou negativos entre 1.79769313486232 x 10E308 e 4.94065645841247 x 10E-324. Son variábeis de punto flotante onde a precisión decimal diminúe cando a parte non decimal aumenta. Son útiles para cálculos precisos. Estes cálculos demoran máis que coas variábeis simples. As variábeis duplas requiren 8 bytes de memoria. O carácter de declaración de tipo é "#".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431				0	gl	Variábel Dim#				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154406				0	gl	Variábel Dim como dupla				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155747				0	gl	Variábeis monetarias				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153337				0	gl	As variábeis monetarias almacénanse internamente como números de 64 bits (8 Bytes) e móstranse como un número decimal fixo con 15 díxitos non decimais e 4 decimais. Os valores varían desde -922337203685477.5808 a +922337203685477.5807. Úsanse para calcular valores monetarios con alta precisión. O carácter de declaración de tipo é "@".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147296				0	gl	Dim Variable@				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	gl	Variábel  Dim como moeda				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148742				0	gl	Variábeis de cadea				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151393				0	gl	As variábeis de cadea almacenan cadeas de ata 65.535 caracteres. Cada carácter almacénase segundo o seu correspondente valor Unicode. Son útiles para o procesamento de textos dentro de programas e para o almacenamento temporal de caracteres non imprimíbeis de ata 64 Kbytes como máximo. A memoria exixida para o almacenamento destas variábeis depende do número de caracteres que conteña. O carácter de declaración de tipo é o "$".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3166467				0	gl	Dim Variabel$				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153027				0	gl	Variábel Dim como cadea				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150534				0	gl	Variábeis booleanas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145632				0	gl	As variábeis booleanas almacenan só un destes valores: VERDADEIRO (TRUE) ou FALSO (FALSE). Un número 0 avalíase como FALSO, mestres que os outros valores avalíanse como VERDADEIRO.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147615				0	gl	Variábel como Booleano				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149722				0	gl	Variábeis de data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159116				0	gl	Date variables can only contain dates and time values stored in an internal format. Values assigned to Date variables with \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030101.xhp\" name=\"Dateserial\"\>\<emph\>Dateserial\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030102.xhp\" name=\"Datevalue\"\>\<emph\>Datevalue\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030205.xhp\" name=\"Timeserial\"\>\<emph\>Timeserial\</emph\>\</link\> or \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030206.xhp\" name=\"Timevalue\"\>\<emph\>Timevalue\</emph\>\</link\> are automatically converted to the internal format. Date-variables are converted to normal numbers by using the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030103.xhp\" name=\"Day\"\>\<emph\>Day\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030104.xhp\" name=\"Month\"\>\<emph\>Month\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030106.xhp\" name=\"Year\"\>\<emph\>Year\</emph\>\</link\> or the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030201.xhp\" name=\"Hour\"\>\<emph\>Hour\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030202.xhp\" name=\"Minute\"\>\<emph\>Minute\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030204.xhp\" name=\"Second\"\>\<emph\>Second\</emph\>\</link\> function. The internal format enables a comparison of date/time values by calculating the difference between two numbers. These variables can only be declared with the key word \<emph\>Date\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150462				0	gl	Variábel Dim como Data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148732				0	gl	Valores iniciais das variábeis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154549				0	gl	Tras declarar a variábel, o seu valor defínese automaticamente como "Nulo". Teña en conta as seguintes convencións:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3143222				0	gl	\<emph\>Numeric\</emph\> variables are automatically assigned the value "0" as soon as they are declared.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	gl	\<emph\>Date variables\</emph\> are assigned the value 0 internally; equivalent to converting the value to "0" with the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030103.xhp\" name=\"Day\"\>\<emph\>Day\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030104.xhp\" name=\"Month\"\>\<emph\>Month\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030106.xhp\" name=\"Year\"\>\<emph\>Year\</emph\>\</link\> or the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030201.xhp\" name=\"Hour\"\>\<emph\>Hour\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030202.xhp\" name=\"Minute\"\>\<emph\>Minute\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030204.xhp\" name=\"Second\"\>\<emph\>Second\</emph\>\</link\> function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154807				0	gl	\<emph\>String variables\</emph\> are assigned an empty-string ("") when they are declared.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153936				0	gl	Matrices				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148736				0	gl	$[officename] Basic recoñece matrices unidimensionais ou multidimensionais definidas por un tipo de variábel especificado. Son útiles para editar listas e táboas en programas. Pode acceder a elementos individuais dunha matriz por medio dun índice numérico.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149546				0	gl	Arrays \<emph\>must\</emph\> be declared with the \<emph\>Dim\</emph\> statement. There are several ways to define the index range of an array:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150143				0	gl	DIM text$(20)				20200411 15:09:53
