helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230				0	gl	When you enter a year using two digits, the corresponding four digit value is determined by a setting in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\>. For example, if 1935 is set as the lower limiting value and you enter 34 as a date value, then the result is 2034 instead of 1934.				20200411 15:09:53
