helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	Importación e exportación HTML				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154380				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>importing; HTML with META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; to HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML; importing META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; META tags in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tags; META tags\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154380				0	gl	Importación e exportación HTML				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	gl	When you export a file to an HTML document, the description and the user-defined file properties are included as META \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tags\"\>tags\</link\> between the HEAD tags of the exported document. META tags are not displayed in a Web browser, and are used to include information, such as keywords for search engines on your Web page. To set the properties of the current document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Description\</emph\> or \<emph\>User Defined\</emph\> tabs, and then type the information you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	gl	As seguintes propiedades convértense en etiquetas META ao exportar un ficheiro como documento HTML:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3154935				0	gl	Propiedade do ficheiro				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	gl	<TITLE>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3153778				0	gl	Asunto				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	gl	<META NAME="CLASSIFICATION" CONTENT="Contido do campo">				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	gl	Palabras chave				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	gl	<META NAME="KEYWORDS" CONTENT="Contido do campo">				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	gl	Descrición				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	gl	<META NAME="DESCRIPTION" CONTENT="Contido do campo">				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	gl	Campos de información 1...4				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3157892				0	gl	<META NAME="Nome do campo de información" CONTENT="Contido do campo">				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855	22			0	gl	Ao importar un documento HTML que contén estas etiquetas META, o contido das mesmas engádese ás caixas de propiedade do ficheiro $[officename] correspondente.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id0926200812164481				0	gl	Keywords must be separated by commas. A keyword can contain white space characters or semicolons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163822				0	gl	Suxestións para a importación				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155307				0	gl	Ao importar un documento HTML, as seguintes etiquetas META convértense automaticamente en campos de $[officename]: <META HTTP-EQUIV="REFRESH"...> e <META NAME="..." ...> , onde NAME corresponde a AUTHOR (AUTOR), CREATED (CREADO), CHANGED (MODIFICADO), CHANGEDBY (MODIFICADO POR), DESCRIPTION (DESCRICIÓN), KEYWORDS (PALABRAS CHAVE) ou CLASSIFICATION (CLASIFICACIÓN).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3146146				0	gl	Os scripts, comentarios e etiquetas META situados inmediatamente antes dunha etiqueta TABLE insírense na primeira cela da táboa.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	gl	Os scripts e etiquetas META situados na cabeceira dun documento HTML impórtanse e ancóranse ao primeiro parágrafo do documento.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	gl	To set the options for importing HTML tags, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>. A known META tag contains either "HTTP-EQUIV" or "NAME", and are imported as $[officename] comments. The only exception is <META NAME="GENERATOR"...>, which is ignored.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163717				0	gl	Suxestións para a exportación				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3159180				0	gl	Comments and script fields at the beginning of the first paragraph in a document are exported to the header of an HTML document. If the document begins with a table, the first paragraph in the first cell of the table is exported to the header of the HTML document.				20200411 15:09:53
