helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148575				0	gl	Parénteses condicionais				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3155312				0	gl	Pódese configurar un formato numérico de xeito que só se aplique caso de que se cumpra a condición especificada. As condicións escríbense entre corchetes [ ].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3159179				0	gl	Pódese utilizar calquera combinación de números e os operadores <, <=, >, >=, = e <>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3159196				0	gl	Por exemplo, para aplicar cores diferentes a datos de temperatura diferentes, introduza:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872				0	gl	[AZUL][<0]#,0 "°C";[VERMELLO][>30]#,0 "°C";[NEGRO]#,0 "°C"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3157870				0	gl	Todas as temperaturas baixo cero están en azul, as temperaturas entre 0 e 30 °C en negro, e as temperaturas superiores a 30 °C en vermello.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154833				0	gl	Números positivos e negativos				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	gl	Para definir un formato numérico que engada un texto diferente a un número dependendo de se é positivo, negativo ou igual a cero, utilice o seguinte formato:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153727				0	gl	0 "positivo"; 0 "negativo"; 0 "cero"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149260				0	gl	Porcentaxes e notación científica				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147218				0	gl	Porcentaxes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168				0	gl	To display numbers as percentages, add the percent sign (%) to the number format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156005				0	gl	Notación científica				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3146923				0	gl	Scientific notation lets you write very large numbers or very small fractions in a compact form. For example, in scientific notation, 650000 is written as 6.5 x 10^5, and 0.000065 as 6.5 x 10^-5. In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>, these numbers are written as 6.5E+5 and 6.5E-5, respectively. To create a number format that displays numbers using scientific notation, enter a # or 0, and then one of the following codes E-, E+, e- or e+.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159080				0	gl	Códigos de formatos numéricos de formatos monetarios.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147318				0	gl	O formato monetario predefinido das celas vén determinado pola configuración rexional do seu sistema operativo mais, se o desexa, pode aplicar símbolos monetarios personalizados as celas. Por exemplo, introduza #,##0,00 € para visualizar 4,50 € (euros).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150032				0	gl	You can also specify the locale setting for the currency by entering the locale code for the country after the symbol. For example, [$€-407] represents Euros in Germany. To view the locale code for a country, select the country in the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> list on the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab of the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157309				0	gl	Formatos de data e de hora				20200411 15:09:53
