helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	gl	\<variable id=\"schriftgroessentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FONTSIZE\"\>Use this dialog to specify the font sizes for your formula. Select a base size and all elements of the formula will be scaled in relation to this base.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146968				0	gl	Tamaño de base				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145115				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:METRICFIELD:RID_FONTSIZEDIALOG:1\"\>All elements of a formula are proportionally scaled to the base size. To change the base size, select or type in the desired point (pt) size. You can also use other units of measure or other \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#metrik\" name=\"metrics\"\>metrics\</link\>, which are then automatically converted to points.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153005				0	gl	To permanently change the default size (12 pt) used in $[officename] Math, you must first set the size (for example, 11 pt) and then click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153735				0	gl	Tamaños relativos				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	gl	Use esta sección para determinar os tamaños relativos de cada tipo de elemento en relación ao tamaño de base.				20200411 15:09:53
