helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	Escala				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>scaling; axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>logarithmic scaling along axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts;scaling axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>X axes;scaling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Y axes; scaling\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868				0	gl	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040201.xhp\" name=\"Scale\"\>Scale\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	gl	Controls the scaling of the X or Y axis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	gl	The axes are automatically scaled by $[officename] so that all values are optimally displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	gl	Para conseguir uns resultados concretos, pode modificar manualmente a escala do eixo. Por exemplo, é posíbel só mostrar as áreas superiores das columnas desprazando a liña cero cara a arriba.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154730				0	gl	Escala				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	gl	You can enter values for subdividing axes in this area. You can automatically set the properties \<emph\>Minimum, Maximum, Major interval, Minor interval count\</emph\> and \<emph\>Reference value\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150751				0	gl	Mínimo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153713				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_MIN\"\>Defines the minimum value for the beginning of the axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156385				0	gl	Máximo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159266				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_MAX\"\>Defines the maximum value for the end of the axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155336				0	gl	Major interval				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3143218				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_STEP_MAIN\"\>Defines the interval for the main division of the axes.\</ahelp\> The main interval cannot be larger than the value area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154020				0	gl	Minor interval count				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_STEP_HELP\"\>Defines the interval for the subdivision of the axes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150089				0	gl	Reference value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_ORIGIN\"\>Specifies at which position to display the values along the axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166432				0	gl	Automático				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE:CBX_AUTO_ORIGIN\"\>You must first deselect the \<emph\>Automatic\</emph\> option in order to modify the values.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149129				0	gl	Desactive esta opción para traballar con valores "fixos", evitando así que se produzan dimensionamentos automáticos.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159206				0	gl	Escala de logaritmos				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145360				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE:CBX_LOGARITHM\"\>Specifies that you want the axis to be subdivided logarithmically.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153956				0	gl	Use este recurso para traballar con valores moi desiguais entre si. A escala logarítmica permite obter espazos idénticos entre as liñas da grade do eixo. Os valores, porén, son variábeis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id9941404				0	gl	Reverse direction				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id5581835				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines where the lower and where the higher values are displayed at the axis. The unchecked state is the mathematical direction.\</ahelp\> That means for Cartesian coordinate systems that the x-axis shows the lower values on the left and the y-axis shows the lower values at the bottom. For polar coordinate systems the mathematical angle axis direction is counterclockwise and the radial axis is from inner to outer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id922204				0	gl	Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id59225				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For some types of axes, you can select to format an axis as text or date, or to detect the type automatically.\</ahelp\> For the axis type "Date" you can set the following options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id1159225				0	gl	Minimum and maximum value to be shown on the ends of the scale.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id2259225				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Resolution can be set to show days, months, or years as interval steps.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3359225				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Major interval can be set to show a certain number of days, months, or years.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id4459225				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Minor interval can be set to show a certain number of days, months, or years.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
