helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147428				0	gl	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Y Error Bars\"\>Y Error Bars\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	gl	\<variable id=\"statistik\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Use the \<emph\>Y Error Bars\</emph\> dialog to display error bars for 2D charts.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3401287				0	gl	An error bar is an indicator line that spans over a range from y - NegativeErrorValue to y + PositiveErrorValue. In this term, y is the value of the data point. When "standard deviation" is selected, y is the mean value of the data series. NegativeErrorValue and PositiveErrorValue are the amounts calculated by the error bar function or given explicitly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	gl	The \<emph\>Insert - Y Error Bars\</emph\> menu command is only available for 2D charts.				20200411 15:09:53
