helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	gl	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the probability value for which the standard logarithmic distribution is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3155820				0	gl	\<emph\>Mean\</emph\> (optional) is the mean value of the standard logarithmic distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3155991				0	gl	\<emph\>StDev\</emph\> (optional) is the standard deviation of the standard logarithmic distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060183.xhp	0	help	par_id3155992				0	gl	\<emph\>Cumulative\</emph\> (optional) = 0 calculates the density function, Cumulative = 1 calculates the distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
