helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	gl	\<emph\>Value1; Value2;...Value30\</emph\> are values or ranges. Text has the value of 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156290				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156446				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAXA(A1;A2;A3;50;100;200;"Text")\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAXA(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153820				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>MEDIAN function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153820				0	gl	MEDIANA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MEDIAN\"\>Returns the median of a set of numbers. In a set containing an uneven number of values, the median will be the number in the middle of the set and in a set containing an even number of values, it will be the mean of the two values in the middle of the set.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148871				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155264				0	gl	MEDIAN(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109				0	gl	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are values or ranges, which represent a sample. Each number can also be replaced by a reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144506				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	gl	for an odd number: \<item type=\"input\"\>=MEDIAN(1;5;9;20;21)\</item\> returns 9 as the median value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	gl	for an even number: \<item type=\"input\"\>=MEDIAN(1;5;9;20)\</item\> returns the average of the two middle values 5 and 9, thus 7.				20200411 15:09:53
