helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148754K1				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>AVERAGEIF function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148754K1				0	gl	AVERAGEIF				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145138K1				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MITTELWERTB\"\>Average the values of cells in a range that meet a criteria.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153326K1				0	gl	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734K1				0	gl	AVERAGEIF( Reference R ; Criterion C [ ; Reference A ] )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260K1				0	gl	 If reference A is omitted, averages the values of cells in the reference range R that meet the Criterion C. If reference A is given, averages the values of cells of a range that is constructed using the top left cell of reference A and applying the dimensions, shape and size, of reference R.  Does not accept constant values as reference parameters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145139K1				0	gl	If no cell in range R matches the Criterion C, an Error is returned. If no Numbers are in the range to be averaged, an Error is returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149504K1				0	gl	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864K1				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=AVERAGEIF(A1:A50;">"0)\</item\>will return the average of A1:A50 of all positive values in the range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148754K2				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>AVERAGEIFS function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148754K2				0	gl	AVERAGEIFS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145138K2				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MITTELWERTC\"\>Average the values of cells that meet multiple criteria in multiple ranges.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153326K2				0	gl	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734K2				0	gl	AVERAGEIFS( Reference A ; Reference R1 ; Criterion C1 [ ; Reference R2 ; Criterion C2 ]... )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260K2				0	gl	Averages the values of cells in the reference range A that meet the Criterion C1 in the reference range R1 and the Criterion C2 in the reference range R2, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145139K2				0	gl	All reference ranges shall have the same dimension and size, else an Error is returned. A logical AND is applied between each array result of each selection; a cell of reference range A is evaluated only if the same position in each array is the result of a Criterion match. If no numbers are in the result set to be averaged, an Error is returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149504K2				0	gl	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864K2				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=AVERAGEIFS(A1:A50;B1:B25;">"0)\</item\>+will return the average of A1:A50 if all cells in the range B1 to B25 are greater than 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153933				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>MODE function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>most common value\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153933				0	gl	MODO				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MODALWERT\"\>Returns the most common value in a data set.\</ahelp\> If there are several values with the same frequency, it returns the smallest value. An error occurs when a value doesn't appear twice.				20200411 15:09:53
