helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145351				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150935				0	gl	NEGBINOMDIST(X; R; SP)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153044				0	gl	\<emph\>X\</emph\> represents the value returned for unsuccessful tests.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151018				0	gl	\<emph\>R\</emph\> represents the value returned for successful tests.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148878				0	gl	\<emph\>SP\</emph\> is the probability of the success of an attempt.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149539				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148770				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NEGBINOMDIST(1;1;0.5)\</item\> returns 0.25.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155516				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>NORMINV function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>normal distribution;inverse of\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
