helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147363				0	gl	The cells for the 1st and 2nd quarters each contain a sum formula for the three cells to their left. If you apply the \<emph\>AutoOutline\</emph\> command, the table is grouped into two quarters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	gl	To remove the outline, select the table, and then choose \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080600.xhp\" name=\"Data - Group and Outline - Remove\"\>Data - Group and Outline - Remove\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	DATEVALUE 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145621				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>DATEVALUE function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145621				0	gl	\<variable id=\"datevalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_datevalue.xhp\"\>DATEVALUE\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145087				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DATWERT\"\>Returns the internal date number for text in quotes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	gl	The internal date number is returned as a number. The number is determined by the date system that is used by $[officename] to calculate dates.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200903491982				0	gl	If the text string also includes a time value, DATEVALUE only returns the integer part of the conversion.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156294				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3149268				0	gl	DATEVALUE("Text")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3154819	23			0	gl	         \<emph\>Text\</emph\> is a valid date expression and must be entered with quotation marks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156309				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155841	25			0	gl	         \<emph\>=DATEVALUE("1954-07-20")\</emph\> yields 19925.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	Protecting Sheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153087				0	gl	Protecting Sheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	gl	\<variable id=\"tabelletext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Protects the cells in the current sheet from being modified.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Choose \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Protect Sheet\</emph\> dialog in which you then specify sheet protection with or without a password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	gl	To protect cells from further editing, the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> check box must be checked on the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020600.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Cell Protection\"\>\<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>\</link\> tab page or on the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	8			0	gl	Unprotected cells or cell ranges can be set up on a protected sheet by using the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> and \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> menus: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	gl	Select the cells that will be unprotected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	gl	Select \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>. Unmark the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156384				0	gl	On the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> menu, activate protection for the sheet. Effective immediately, only the cell range you selected in step 1 can be edited.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149566	9			0	gl	To later change an unprotected area to a protected area, select the range. Next, on the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> tab page, check the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box. Finally, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet \</emph\>menu. The previously editable range is now protected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153964				0	gl	Sheet protection also affects the context menu of the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen. The \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> and \<emph\>Rename\</emph\> commands cannot be selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150301				0	gl	If a sheet is protected, you will not be able to modify or delete any Cell Styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	gl	A protected sheet or cell range can no longer be modified until this protection is disabled. To disable the protection, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> command. If no password was set, the sheet protection is immediately disabled. If the sheet was password protected, the \<emph\>Remove Protection\</emph\> dialog opens, where you must enter the password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149815				0	gl	Once saved, protected sheets can only be saved again by using the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150206				0	gl	Contrasinal (opcional)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Allows you to enter a password to protect the sheet from unauthorized changes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148700				0	gl	Complete protection of your work can be achieved by combining both options on the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\> menu, including password protection. To prohibit opening the document altogether, in the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> dialog mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> box before you click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	Mark Invalid Data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153821				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>cells; invalid data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; showing invalid data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>invalid data;marking\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153821				0	gl	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030800.xhp\" name=\"Mark Invalid Data\"\>Mark Invalid Data\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowInvalid\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Marks all cells in the sheet that contain values outside the validation rules.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	gl	The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120000.xhp\" name=\"validity rules\"\>validity rules\</link\> restrict the input of numbers, dates, time values and text to certain values. However, it is possible to enter invalid values or copy invalid values into the cells if the \<emph\>Stop\</emph\> option is not selected. When you assign a validity rule, existing values in a cell will not be modified.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	DOMINGOPASCUA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152960				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>EASTERSUNDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152960				0	gl	\<variable id=\"eastersunday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_eastersunday.xhp\"\>EASTERSUNDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154570				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_OSTERSONNTAG\"\>Returns the date of Easter Sunday for the entered year.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	hd_id9460127				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id2113711				0	gl	EASTERSUNDAY(Year)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3938413				0	gl	\<emph\>Year\</emph\> is an integer between 1583 and 9956 or 0 and 99. You can also calculate other holidays by simple addition with this date.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	gl	Easter Monday = EASTERSUNDAY(Year) + 1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3147521				0	gl	Good Friday = EASTERSUNDAY(Year) - 2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3146072				0	gl	Pentecost Sunday = EASTERSUNDAY(Year) + 49				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149553				0	gl	Pentecost Monday = EASTERSUNDAY(Year) + 50				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155120				0	gl	Exemplos				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154472				0	gl	=EASTERSUNDAY(2000) returns 2000-04-23.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150940				0	gl	EASTERSUNDAY(2000)+49 returns the internal serial number 36688. The result is 2000-06-11. Format the serial date number as a date, for example in the format YYYY-MM-DD.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	Alerta de erro				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153821				0	gl	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120300.xhp\" name=\"Error Alert\"\>Error Alert\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:TABPAGE:TP_VALIDATION_ERROR\"\>Define the error message that is displayed when invalid data is entered in a cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	gl	You can also start a macro with an error message. A sample macro is provided at the end of this page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280				0	gl	Show error message when invalid values are entered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150768				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays the error message that you enter in the \<emph\>Contents\</emph\> area when invalid data is entered in a cell.\</ahelp\> If enabled, the message is displayed to prevent an invalid entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146984	5			0	gl	In both cases, if you select "Stop", the invalid entry is deleted and the previous value is reentered in the cell. The same applies if you close the "Warning" and "Information" dialogs by clicking the \<emph\>Cancel \</emph\>button. If you close the dialogs with the \<emph\>OK\</emph\> button, the invalid entry is not deleted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152460				0	gl	Contido				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148646				0	gl	Acción				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3151115				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:TP_VALIDATION_ERROR:LB_ACTION\"\>Select the action that you want to occur when invalid data is entered in a cell.\</ahelp\> The "Stop" action rejects the invalid entry and displays a dialog that you have to close by clicking \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The "Warning" and "Information" actions display a dialog that can be closed by clicking \<emph\>OK\</emph\> or \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>. The invalid entry is only rejected when you click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156441				0	gl	Explorar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153160				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:PUSHBUTTON:TP_VALIDATION_ERROR:BTN_SEARCH\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Macro\"\>Macro\</link\> dialog where you can select the macro that is executed when invalid data is entered in a cell. The macro is executed after the error message is displayed.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
