helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3158423				0	gl	RATE(NPer; Pmt; PV; FV; Type; Guess)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148910				0	gl	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods, during which payments are made (payment period).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148925				0	gl	\<emph\>Pmt\</emph\> is the constant payment (annuity) paid during each period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149160				0	gl	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the cash value in the sequence of payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3166456				0	gl	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the future value, which is reached at the end of the periodic payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153243				0	gl	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) is the due date of the periodic payment, either at the beginning or at the end of a period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146949				0	gl	\<emph\>Guess\</emph\> (optional) determines the estimated value of the interest with iterative calculation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E2A				0	gl	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149791				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150706				0	gl	What is the constant interest rate for a payment period of 3 periods if 10 currency units are paid regularly and the present cash value is 900 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RATE(3;10;900)\</item\> = -121% The interest rate is therefore 121%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149106				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>INTRATE function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149106				0	gl	TAXAXUROS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149918				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_INTRATE\"\>Calculates the annual interest rate that results when a security (or other item) is purchased at an investment value and sold at a redemption value. No interest is paid.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
