helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	gl	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146126				0	gl	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153705				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530				0	gl	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how many days are there in the interest period in which the settlement date falls?				20200411 15:09:53
