helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146800				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146813				0	gl	What is the value at the end of an investment if the interest rate is 4% and the payment period is two years, with a periodic payment of 750 currency units. The investment has a present value of 2,500 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149302				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FV(4%;2;750;2500) \</item\>= -4234.00 currency units. The value at the end of the investment is 4234.00 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155912				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>FVSCHEDULE function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>future values;varying interest rates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155912				0	gl	VFPROGRAMA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3163726				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_FVSCHEDULE\"\>Calculates the accumulated value of the starting capital for a series of periodically varying interest rates.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149571				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148891				0	gl	FVSCHEDULE(Principal; Schedule)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148904				0	gl	\<emph\>Principal\</emph\> is the starting capital.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148562				0	gl	\<emph\>Schedule\</emph\> is a series of interest rates, for example, as a range H3:H5 or as a (List) (see example).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147288				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148638				0	gl	1000 currency units have been invested in for three years. The interest rates were 3%, 4% and 5% per annum. What is the value after three years?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156358				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FVSCHEDULE(1000;{0.03;0.04;0.05})\</item\> returns 1124.76.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156435				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;number of payment periods\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>payment periods;number of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of payment periods\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>NPER function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156435				0	gl	NPER				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZZR\"\>Returns the number of periods for an investment based on periodic, constant payments and a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147216				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155934				0	gl	NPER(Rate; Pmt; PV; FV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155946				0	gl	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149042				0	gl	\<emph\>Pmt\</emph\> is the constant annuity paid in each period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153134				0	gl	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present value (cash value) in a sequence of payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398				0	gl	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the future value, which is reached at the end of the last period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145127				0	gl	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) is the due date of the payment at the beginning or at the end of the period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN1166C				0	gl	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155795				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147378				0	gl	How many payment periods does a payment period cover with a periodic interest rate of 6%, a periodic payment of 153.75 currency units and a present cash value of 2.600 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156171				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NPER(6%;153.75;2600)\</item\> = -12,02. The payment period covers 12.02 periods.				20200411 15:09:53
