helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155802				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>COMBIN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of combinations\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155802				0	gl	COMBINAR				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156172				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KOMBINATIONEN\"\>Returns the number of combinations for elements without repetition.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223				0	gl	COMBIN(Count1; Count2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150313				0	gl	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153830				0	gl	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6807458				0	gl	COMBIN returns the number of ordered ways to choose these items. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 3 different ways, namely AB, AC and BC.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7414471				0	gl	COMBIN implements the formula: Count1!/(Count2!*(Count1-Count2)!)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153171				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153517				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COMBIN(3;2)\</item\> returns 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150284				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>COMBINA function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of combinations with repetitions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150284				0	gl	COMBINAR2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157894				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KOMBINATIONEN2\"\>Returns the number of combinations of a subset of items including repetitions.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145752				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145765				0	gl	COMBINA(Count1; Count2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153372				0	gl	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155544				0	gl	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1997131				0	gl	COMBINA returns the number of unique ways to choose these items, where the order of choosing is irrelevant, and repetition of items is allowed. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 6 different ways, namely AA, AB, AC, BB, BC and CC.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2052064				0	gl	COMBINA implements the formula: (Count1+Count2-1)! / (Count2!(Count1-1)!)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154584				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152904				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COMBINA(3;2)\</item\> returns 6.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156086				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>TRUNC function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places;cutting off\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156086				0	gl	TRUNCAR				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157866				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KUERZEN\"\>Truncates a number by removing decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148499				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148511				0	gl	TRUNC(Number; Count)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150796				0	gl	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> with at most \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. Excess decimal places are simply removed, irrespective of sign.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150816				0	gl	\<item type=\"literal\"\>TRUNC(Number; 0)\</item\> behaves as \<item type=\"literal\"\>INT(Number)\</item\> for positive numbers, but effectively rounds towards zero for negative numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148548				0	gl	The \<emph\>visible\</emph\> decimal places of the result are specified in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152555				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152569				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TRUNC(1.239;2)\</item\> returns 1.23. The 9 is lost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7050080				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TRUNC(-1.234999;3)\</item\> returns -1.234. All the 9s are lost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153601				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>LN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>natural logarithm\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153601				0	gl	LN				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154974				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LN\"\>Returns the natural logarithm based on the constant e of a number.\</ahelp\> The constant e has a value of approximately 2.71828182845904.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154993				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155284				0	gl	LN(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155297				0	gl	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose natural logarithm is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153852				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153866				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LN(3)\</item\> returns the natural logarithm of 3 (approximately 1.0986).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5747245				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LN(EXP(321))\</item\> returns 321.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109813				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>LOG function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>logarithms\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109813				0	gl	LOG				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3109841				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG\"\>Returns the logarithm of a number to the specified base.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144719				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144732				0	gl	LOG(Number; Base)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144746				0	gl	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose logarithm is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152840				0	gl	\<emph\>Base\</emph\> (optional) is the base for the logarithm calculation. If omitted, Base 10 is assumed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152860				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154429				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG(10;3)\</item\> returns the logarithm to base 3 of 10 (approximately 2.0959).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5577562				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG(7^4;7)\</item\> returns 4.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154187				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>LOG10 function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>base-10 logarithm\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154187				0	gl	LOG10				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155476				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG10\"\>Returns the base-10 logarithm of a number.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155494				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159294				0	gl	LOG10(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159308				0	gl	Returns the logarithm to base 10 of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159328				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157916				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG10(5)\</item\> returns the base-10 logarithm of 5 (approximately 0.69897).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152518				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>CEILING function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding;up to multiples of significance\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152518				0	gl	LÍMITESUPERIOR				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153422				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_OBERGRENZE\"\>Rounds a number up to the nearest multiple of Significance.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153440				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153454				0	gl	CEILING(Number; Significance; Mode)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153467				0	gl	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be rounded up.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155000				0	gl	\<emph\>Significance\</emph\> is the number to whose multiple the value is to be rounded up.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155020				0	gl	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional value. If the Mode value is given and not equal to zero, and if Number and Significance are negative, then rounding is done based on the absolute value of Number. This parameter is ignored when exporting to MS Excel as Excel does not know any third parameter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163792				0	gl	If both parameters Number and Significance are negative and the Mode value is equal to zero or is not given, the results in $[officename] and Excel will differ after the import has been completed. If you export the spreadsheet to Excel, use Mode=1 to see the same results in Excel as in Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145697				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145710				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2)\</item\> returns -10				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145725				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2;0)\</item\> returns -10				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145740				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2;1)\</item\> returns -12				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157762				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>PI function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157762				0	gl	PI				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157790				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PI\"\>Returns 3.14159265358979, the value of the mathematical constant PI to 14 decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157809				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157822				0	gl	PI()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157836				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152370				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PI()\</item\> returns 3.14159265358979.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152418				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>MULTINOMIAL function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152418				0	gl	MULTINOMIAL				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152454				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_MULTINOMIAL\"\> Returns the factorial of the sum of the arguments divided by the product of the factorials of the arguments.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155646				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155660				0	gl	MULTINOMIAL(Number(s))				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155673				0	gl	\<emph\>Number(s)\</emph\> is a list of up to 30 numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155687				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155701				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MULTINOMIAL(F11:H11)\</item\> returns 1260, if F11 to H11 contain the values \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>, \<item type=\"input\"\>3\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\>. This corresponds to the formula =(2+3+4)! / (2!*3!*4!)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155717				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>POWER function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155717				0	gl	POTENCIA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159495				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_POTENZ\"\>Returns a number raised to another number.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159513				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159526				0	gl	POWER(Base; Exponent)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159540				0	gl	Returns \<emph\>Base\</emph\> raised to the power of \<emph\>Exponent\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5081637				0	gl	The same result may be achieved by using the exponentiation operator ^:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9759514				0	gl	\<item type=\"literal\"\>Base^Exponent\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159580				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159594				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=POWER(4;3)\</item\> returns 64, which is 4 to the power of 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1614429				0	gl	=4^3 also returns 4 to the power of 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152651				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>SERIESSUM function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152651				0	gl	SUMARSECUENCIA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152688				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sums the first terms of a power series.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152708				0	gl	SERIESSUM(x;n;m;coefficients) = coefficient_1*x^n + coefficient_2*x^(n+m) + coefficient_3*x^(n+2m) +...+ coefficient_i*x^(n+(i-1)m)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152724				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_idN11BD9				0	gl	SERIESSUM(X; N; M; Coefficients)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152737				0	gl	\<emph\>X\</emph\> is the input value for the power series.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144344				0	gl	\<emph\>N\</emph\> is the initial power				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144357				0	gl	\<emph\>M\</emph\> is the increment to increase N				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144370				0	gl	\<emph\>Coefficients\</emph\> is a series of coefficients. For each coefficient the series sum is extended by one section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144386				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>PRODUCT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers;multiplying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiplying;numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144386				0	gl	PRODUTO				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144414				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PRODUKT\"\>Multiplies all the numbers given as arguments and returns the product.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144433				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144446				0	gl	PRODUCT(Number1; Number2; ...; Number30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144460				0	gl	\<emph\>Number1 to 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments whose product is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1589098				0	gl	PRODUCT returns number1 * number2 * number3 * ...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144480				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144494				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PRODUCT(2;3;4)\</item\> returns 24.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3160340				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>SUMSQ function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>square number additions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sums;of square numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160340				0	gl	SUMARCAD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160368				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUADRATESUMME\"\>If you want to calculate the sum of the squares of numbers (totaling up of the squares of the arguments), enter these into the text fields.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160388				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160402				0	gl	SUMSQ(Number1; Number2; ...; Number30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160415				0	gl	\<emph\>Number1 to 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments the sum of whose squares is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160436				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160449				0	gl	If you enter the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>; \<item type=\"input\"\>3\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\> in the Number 1; 2 and 3 text boxes, 29 is returned as the result.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158247				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>MOD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remainders of divisions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158247				0	gl	RESTO				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158276				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_REST\"\>Returns the remainder when one integer is divided by another.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158294				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158308				0	gl	MOD(Dividend; Divisor)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158321				0	gl	 For integer arguments this function returns Dividend modulo Divisor, that is the remainder when \<emph\>Dividend\</emph\> is divided by \<emph\>Divisor\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158341				0	gl	This function is implemented as \<item type=\"literal\"\>Dividend - Divisor * INT(Dividend/Divisor)\</item\> , and this formula gives the result if the arguments are not integer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158361				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158374				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MOD(22;3)\</item\> returns 1, the remainder when 22 is divided by 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1278420				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MOD(11.25;2.5)\</item\> returns 1.25.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144592				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>QUOTIENT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>divisions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144592				0	gl	COCIENTE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144627				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_QUOTIENT\"\>Returns the integer part of a division operation.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144646				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144659				0	gl	QUOTIENT(Numerator; Denominator)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	gl	Returns the integer part of \<emph\>Numerator\</emph\> divided by \<emph\>Denominator\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7985168				0	gl	QUOTIENT is equivalent to \<item type=\"literal\"\>INT(numerator/denominator)\</item\>, except that it may report errors with different error codes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144674				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144687				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=QUOTIENT(11;3)\</item\> returns 3. The remainder of 2 is lost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144702				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>RADIANS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;degrees, into radians\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144702				0	gl	RADIÁNS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158025				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RAD\"\>Converts degrees to radians.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158042				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158055				0	gl	RADIANS(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158069				0	gl	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the angle in degrees to be converted to radians.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id876186				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RADIANS(90)\</item\> returns 1.5707963267949, which is PI/2 to Calc's accuracy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158121				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>ROUND function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158121				0	gl	ARREDONDAR				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158150				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number to a certain number of decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158169				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158182				0	gl	ROUND(Number; Count)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158196				0	gl	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds to the nearest integer. If Count is negative, the function rounds to the nearest 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id599688				0	gl	This function rounds to the nearest number. See ROUNDDOWN and ROUNDUP for alternatives.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145863				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145876				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(2.348;2)\</item\> returns 2.35				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145899				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(-32.4834;3)\</item\> returns -32.483. Change the cell format to see all decimals.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1371501				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(2.348;0)\</item\> returns 2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id4661702				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(2.5)\</item\> returns 3. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7868892				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(987.65;-2)\</item\> returns 1000.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145991				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>ROUNDDOWN function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145991				0	gl	ARREDONDARCARAAABAIXO				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146020				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ABRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number down, toward zero, to a certain precision.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146037				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146051				0	gl	ROUNDDOWN(Number; Count)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146064				0	gl	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded down (towards zero) to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds down to an integer. If Count is negative, the function rounds down to the next 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	gl	This function rounds towards zero. See ROUNDUP and ROUND for alternatives.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163164				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163178				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(1.234;2)\</item\> returns 1.23.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5833307				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(45.67;0)\</item\> returns 45.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7726676				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(-45.67)\</item\> returns -45.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3729361				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(987.65;-2)\</item\> returns 900.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163268				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>ROUNDUP function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163268				0	gl	ARREDONDARCARAAARRIBA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163297				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_AUFRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number up, away from zero, to a certain precision.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163315				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163328				0	gl	ROUNDUP(Number; Count)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163342				0	gl	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded up (away from zero) to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds up to an integer. If Count is negative, the function rounds up to the next 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9573961				0	gl	This function rounds away from zero. See ROUNDDOWN and ROUND for alternatives.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163381				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144786				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(1.1111;2)\</item\> returns 1.12.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7700430				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(1.2345;1)\</item\> returns 1.3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1180455				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(45.67;0)\</item\> returns 46.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3405560				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(-45.67)\</item\> returns -46.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3409527				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(987.65;-2)\</item\> returns 1000.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144877				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>SIN function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144877				0	gl	SENO				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144906				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SIN\"\>Returns the sine of the given angle (in radians).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144923				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144937				0	gl	SIN(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144950				0	gl	Returns the (trigonometric) sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, the angle in radians.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8079470				0	gl	To return the sine of an angle in degrees, use the RADIANS function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144969				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144983				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SIN(PI()/2)\</item\> returns 1, the sine of PI/2 radians.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3916440				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SIN(RADIANS(30))\</item\> returns 0.5, the sine of 30 degrees.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163397				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>SINH function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163397				0	gl	SENOH				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163426				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SINHYP\"\>Returns the hyperbolic sine of a number.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163444				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163457				0	gl	SINH(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163471				0	gl	Returns the hyperbolic sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163491				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163504				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SINH(0)\</item\> returns 0, the hyperbolic sine of 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163596				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>SUM function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;numbers in cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163596				0	gl	SUMA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163625				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMME\"\>Adds all the numbers in a range of cells.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163643				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163656				0	gl	SUM(Number1; Number2; ...; Number30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163671				0	gl	\<emph\>Number 1 to Number 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments whose sum is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163690				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163704				0	gl	If you enter the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>; \<item type=\"input\"\>3 \</item\>and \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\> in the Number 1; 2 and 3 text boxes, 9 will be returned as the result.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151740				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM(A1;A3;B5)\</item\> calculates the sum of the three cells. \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM (A1:E10)\</item\> calculates the sum of all cells in the A1 to E10 cell range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151756				0	gl	Conditions linked by AND can be used with the function SUM() in the following manner:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151774				0	gl	Example assumption: You have entered invoices into a table. Column A contains the date value of the invoice, column B the amounts. You want to find a formula that you can use to return the total of all amounts only for a specific month, e.g. only the amount for the period >=2008-01-01 to <2008-02-01. The range with the date values covers A1:A40, the range containing the amounts to be totaled is B1:B40. C1 contains the start date, 2008\<item type=\"input\"\>-01-01\</item\>, of the invoices to be included and C2 the date, 2008\<item type=\"input\"\>-02-01\</item\>, that is no longer included.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151799				0	gl	Enter the following formula as an array formula:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151813				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM((A1:A40>=C1)*(A1:A40<C2)*B1:B40)\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151828				0	gl	In order to enter this as an array formula, you must press the Shift\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>+Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>+ Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+ Enter keys instead of simply pressing the Enter key to close the formula. The formula will then be shown in the \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> bar enclosed in braces.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151869				0	gl	{=SUM((A1:A40>=C1)*(A1:A40<C2)*B1:B40)}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151884				0	gl	The formula is based on the fact that the result of a comparison is 1 if the criterion is met and 0 if it is not met. The individual comparison results will be treated as an array and used in matrix multiplication, and at the end the individual values will be totaled to give the result matrix.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151957				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>SUMIF function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;specified numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151957				0	gl	SUMARSE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151986				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMMEWENN\"\>Adds the cells specified by a given criteria.\</ahelp\> This function is used to browse a range when you search for a certain value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152015				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152028				0	gl	SUMIF(Range; Criteria; SumRange)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152043				0	gl	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range to which the criteria are to be applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152062				0	gl	\<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> is the cell in which the search criterion is shown, or the search criterion itself. If the criteria is written into the formula, it has to be surrounded by double quotes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152083				0	gl	\<emph\>SumRange\</emph\> is the range from which values are summed. If this parameter has not been indicated, the values found in the Range are summed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8347422				0	gl	SUMIF supports the reference concatenation operator (~) only in the Criteria parameter, and only if the optional SumRange parameter is not given.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152110				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152148				0	gl	To sum up only negative numbers: \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIF(A1:A10;"<0")\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6670125				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIF(A1:A10;">0";B1:10)\</item\> - sums values from the range B1:B10 only if the corresponding values in the range A1:A10 are >0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196				0	gl	See COUNTIF() for some more syntax examples that can be used with SUMIF().				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151957K				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>SUMIFS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;specified numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151957K				0	gl	SUMIFS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151986K				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMMEWNRNG\"\>Sum the values of cells in a range that meet multiple criteria in multiple ranges.\</ahelp\> 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152015K				0	gl	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152028K				0	gl	SUMIFS( Reference R ; Reference R1 ; Criterion C1 [ ; Reference R2 ; Criterion C2 ]... )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152043K				0	gl	Sums the value of cells in range R that meet the Criterion C1 in the reference range R1, and the Criterion C2 in the reference range R2, and so on. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152062K				0	gl	A \<emph\>Criterion\</emph\> is a single cell Reference, Number or Text. If the criterion is written into the formula, it has to be surrounded by double quotes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152083K				0	gl	All \<emph\>Reference\</emph\> ranges shall have the same dimension and size, else an Error is returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152110K				0	gl	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152148K				0	gl	Sum up cells in range A1:10 if the entries in B1:B10 are positive, and the entries in D1:D10 are the letter "A": \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIFS(A1:A10;B1:B10;">0";D1:D10;"A")\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196K				0	gl	See COUNTIFS() for some more syntax examples that can be used with SUMIFS().				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152195				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>TAN function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152195				0	gl	TAN				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152224				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TAN\"\>Returns the tangent of the given angle (in radians).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152242				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152255				0	gl	TAN(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152269				0	gl	Returns the (trigonometric) tangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, the angle in radians.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5752128				0	gl	To return the tangent of an angle in degrees, use the RADIANS function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152287				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152301				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TAN(PI()/4) \</item\>returns 1, the tangent of PI/4 radians.				20200411 15:09:53
