helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164596				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_SQRTPI\"\>Returns the square root of (PI times a number).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164614				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164627				0	gl	SQRTPI(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1501510				0	gl	Returns the positive square root of (PI multiplied by \<emph\>Number\</emph\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9929197				0	gl	This is equivalent to \<item type=\"literal\"\>SQRT(PI()*Number)\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164641				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164654				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SQRTPI(2)\</item\> returns the squareroot of (2PI), approximately 2.506628.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164669				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>random numbers; between limits\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>RANDBETWEEN function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164669				0	gl	ALEATORIOENTRE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164711				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_RANDBETWEEN\"\>Returns an integer random number in a specified range.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164745				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164758				0	gl	RANDBETWEEN(Bottom; Top)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7112338				0	gl	Returns an integer random number between integers \<emph\>Bottom\</emph\> and \<emph\>Top\</emph\> (both inclusive).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2855616				0	gl	This function produces a new random number each time Calc recalculates. To force Calc to recalculate manually press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2091433				0	gl	To generate random numbers which never recalculate, copy cells containing this function, and use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste Special\</item\> (with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paste All\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formulas\</item\> not marked and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> marked).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164772				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164785				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RANDBETWEEN(20;30)\</item\> returns an integer of between 20 and 30.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164800				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>RAND function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>random numbers;between 0 and 1\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164800				0	gl	ALEATORIO				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164829				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZUFALLSZAHL\"\>Returns a random number between 0 and 1.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164870				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164884				0	gl	RAND()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5092318				0	gl	This function produces a new random number each time Calc recalculates. To force Calc to recalculate manually press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9312417				0	gl	To generate random numbers which never recalculate, copy cells each containing =RAND(), and use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste Special\</item\> (with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paste All\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formulas\</item\> not marked and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> marked).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id9089022				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9569078				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RAND()\</item\> returns a random number between 0 and 1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164897				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTIF function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>counting;specified cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164897				0	gl	CONTARSE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164926				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZAEHLENWENN\"\>Returns the number of cells that meet with certain criteria within a cell range.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164953				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164967				0	gl	COUNTIF(Range; Criteria)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164980				0	gl	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range to which the criteria are to be applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165000				0	gl	\<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> indicates the criteria in the form of a number, an expression or a character string. These criteria determine which cells are counted. You may also enter a search text in the form of a regular expression, e.g. b.* for all words that begin with b. You may also indicate a cell range that contains the search criterion. If you search for literal text, enclose the text in double quotes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165037				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166505				0	gl	A1:A10 is a cell range containing the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2000\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>2009\</item\>. Cell B1 contains the number \<item type=\"input\"\>2006\</item\>. In cell B2, you enter a formula:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3581652				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;2006)\</item\> - this returns 1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id708639				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;B1)\</item\> - this returns 1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;">=2006") \</item\>- this returns 4				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2118594				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;"<"&B1)\</item\> - when B1 contains \<item type=\"input\"\>2006\</item\>, this returns 6				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id166020				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;C2)\</item\> where cell C2 contains the text \<item type=\"input\"\>>2006\</item\> counts the number of cells in the range A1:A10 which are >2006 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6386913				0	gl	To count only negative numbers: \<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;"<0")\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164897K				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTIFS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>counting;specified cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164897K				0	gl	COUNTIFS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164926K				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZAEHLENWNRNG\"\>Count the number of cells that meet multiple criteria in multiple ranges.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164953K				0	gl	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164967K				0	gl	COUNTIFS( Reference R1 ; Criterion C1 [ ; Reference R2 ; Criterion C2 ]... )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164980K				0	gl	\<emph\>Reference R1\</emph\> is the  range to which the \<emph\>Criterion C1\</emph\>applies. \<emph\>Reference R2\</emph\> is the  range to which the \<emph\>Criterion C2\</emph\>applies, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165000K				0	gl	All \<emph\>Reference \</emph\> ranges shall have the same dimension and size, else an Error is returned. \<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> indicates the criteria in the form of a number, an expression or a character string. These criteria determine which cells are counted. You may also enter a search text in the form of a regular expression, e.g. b.* for all words that begin with b. You may also indicate a cell range that contains the search criterion. If you search for literal text, enclose the text in double quotes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165037K				0	gl	Examples:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166505K				0	gl	A1:A10 is a cell range containing the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2000\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>2009\</item\>. B1:B10 is a cell range containing the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2007\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>2016\</item\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3581652K				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIFS(A1:A10;2006;B1:B10;2014)\</item\> - this returns 2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225K				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIFS(A1:A10;">=2006";B1:B10;">=2006") \</item\>- this returns 14				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	Máis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148492				0	gl	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040201.xhp\" name=\"More\"\>More\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400				0	gl	\<variable id=\"zusaetzetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SC:MOREBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_MORE\"\>Shows additional filter options.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	gl	Opcións				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154138				0	gl	Diferenciar maiúsculas de minúsculas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_CASE\"\>Distinguishes between uppercase and lowercase letters when filtering the data.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154908				0	gl	Contén etiquetas de columna				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_HEADER\"\>Includes the column labels in the first row of a cell range.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155306				0	gl	Copiar resultados a				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:ED_COPY_AREA\"\>Select the check box, and then select the cell range where you want to display the filter results.\</ahelp\> You can also select a named range from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272				0	gl	Expresión regular				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_REGEXP\"\>Allows you to use wildcards in the filter definition.\</ahelp\> For a list of the regular expressions that $[officename] supports, click \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"here\"\>here\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	gl	If the \<emph\>Regular Expressions\</emph\> check box is selected, you can use regular expressions in the Value field if the Condition list box is set to '=' EQUAL or '<>' UNEQUAL. This also applies to the respective cells that you reference for an advanced filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149958				0	gl	No duplication				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_UNIQUE\"\>Excludes duplicate rows in the list of filtered data.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154018				0	gl	Keep filter criteria				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_FILTER:BTN_DEST_PERS\"\>Select the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> check box, and then specify the destination range where you want to display the filtered data. If this box is checked, the destination range remains linked to the source range. You must have defined the source range under \<emph\>Data - Define range\</emph\> as a database range.\</ahelp\> Following this, you can reapply the defined filter at any time as follows: click into the source range, then choose \<emph\>Data - Refresh Range\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	gl	Intervalo de datos				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	gl	Displays the cell range or the name of the cell range that you want to filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	DÍAÚTIL				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149012				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>WORKDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149012				0	gl	\<variable id=\"workday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_workday.xhp\"\>WORKDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149893				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_WORKDAY\"\> The result is a date number that can be formatted as a date. You then see the date of a day that is a certain number of \<emph\>workdays\</emph\> away from the \<emph\>start date\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146944				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844				0	gl	WORKDAY(StartDate; Days; Holidays)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3147469				0	gl	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is the date from when the calculation is carried out. If the start date is a workday, the day is included in the calculation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153038				0	gl	\<emph\>Days\</emph\> is the number of workdays. Positive value for a result after the start date, negative value for a result before the start date.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	gl	\<emph\>Holidays\</emph\> is a list of optional holidays. These are non-working days. Enter a cell range in which the holidays are listed individually.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150141				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3152782				0	gl	What date came 17 workdays after 1 December 2001? Enter the start date "2001-12-01" in C3 and the number of workdays in D3. Cells F3 to J3 contain the following Christmas and New Year holidays: "2001-12-24", "2001-12-25", "2001-12-26", "2001-12-31", "2002-01-01".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3146142				0	gl	=WORKDAY(C3;D3;F3:J3) returns 2001-12-28. Format the serial date number as a date, for example in the format YYYY-MM-DD.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	Agrupar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153088				0	gl	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080300.xhp\" name=\"Group\"\>Group\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	gl	\<variable id=\"gruppierung\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Group\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Defines the selected cell range as a group of rows or columns.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069	3			0	gl	When you group a cell range, and outline icon appears in the margins next to the group. To hide or show the group, click the icon. To ungroup the selection, choose \<emph\>Data – Outline -\</emph\> \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080400.xhp\" name=\"Ungroup\"\>\<emph\>Ungroup\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	gl	Incluír				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150448				0	gl	Filas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_GROUP_ROWS\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Groups the selected rows.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145786				0	gl	Columnas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146984				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_GROUP_COLS\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Groups the selected columns.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	Combinar celas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149785				0	gl	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05060000.xhp\" name=\"Merge Cells\"\>Merge Cells\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151246				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Combines the selected cells into a single cell or splits merged cells.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	gl	The merged cell receives the name of the first cell of the original cell range. Merged cells cannot be merged a second time with other cells. The range must form a rectangle, multiple selection is not supported.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149665				0	gl	If the cells to be merged have any contents, a security dialog is shown.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	Multiple Operations				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153381				0	gl	Multiple Operations				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	gl	\<variable id=\"mehrfachoperationen\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:TableOperationDialog\"\>Applies the same formula to different cells, but with different parameter values.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152598				0	gl	The \<emph\>Row\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column\</emph\> box must contain a reference to the first cell of the selected range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	gl	If you export a spreadsheet containing multiple operations to Microsoft Excel, the location of the cells containing the formula must be fully defined relative to the data range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156441				0	gl	Predefinicións				20200411 15:09:53
