helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RMZ\"\>Returns the periodic payment for an annuity with constant interest rates.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145257				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147278				0	gl	PMT(Rate; NPer; PV; FV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147291				0	gl	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148641				0	gl	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the number of periods in which annuity is paid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156360				0	gl	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present value (cash value) in a sequence of payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154920				0	gl	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the desired value (future value) to be reached at the end of the periodic payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156434				0	gl	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) is the due date for the periodic payments. Type=1 is payment at the beginning and Type=0 is payment at the end of each period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_idN11645				0	gl	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152358				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	gl	What are the periodic payments at a yearly interest rate of 1.99% if the payment time is 3 years and the cash value is 25,000 currency units. There are 36 months as 36 payment periods, and the interest rate per payment period is 1.99%/12.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155943				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PMT(1.99%/12;36;25000)\</item\> = -715.96 currency units. The periodic monthly payment is therefore 715.96 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155799				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>TBILLEQ function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>treasury bills;annual return\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>annual return on treasury bills\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155799				0	gl	LETTESEQ				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154403				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_TBILLEQ\"\>Calculates the annual return on a treasury bill ().\</ahelp\> A treasury bill is purchased on the settlement date and sold at the full par value on the maturity date, that must fall within the same year. A discount is deducted from the purchase price.				20200411 15:09:53
