helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154261				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBMIN\"\>DMIN returns the minimum content of a cell (field) in a database that matches the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147238				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148479				0	gl	DMIN(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151050				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148925				0	gl	To find the shortest distance to school for the children in each grade in the above example (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149161				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DMIN(A1:E10;"Distance to School";A13:E14)\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148917				0	gl	In row 14, under Grade, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>1, 2, 3,\</item\> and so on, one after the other. The shortest distance to school for each grade appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154274				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>DAVERAGE function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>averages; in Calc databases\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>calculating;averages in Calc databases\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154274				0	gl	BDMEDIA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3166453				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBMITTELWERT\"\>DAVERAGE returns the average of the values of all cells (fields) in all rows (database records) that match the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146955				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150710				0	gl	DAVERAGE(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152943				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149104				0	gl	To find the average weight of all children of the same age in the above example (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153688				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DAVERAGE(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155587				0	gl	In row 14, under Age, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>7, 8, 9,\</item\> and so on, one after the other. The average weight of all children of the same age appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159269				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>DPRODUCT function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>multiplying;cell contents in Calc databases\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159269				0	gl	BDPRODUTO				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152879				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBPRODUKT\"\>DPRODUCT multiplies all cells of a data range where the cell contents match the search criteria.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149966				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154854				0	gl	DPRODUCT(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149802				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148986				0	gl	With the birthday party example above (scroll up, please), there is no meaningful application of this function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148462				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>DSTDEV function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>standard deviations in databases;based on a sample\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148462				0	gl	BDDESVEST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154605				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBSTDABW\"\>DSTDEV calculates the standard deviation of a population based on a sample, using the numbers in a database column that match the given conditions.\</ahelp\> The records are treated as a sample of data. That means that the children in the example represent a cross section of all children. Note that a representative result can not be obtained from a sample of less than one thousand.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149427				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148661				0	gl	DSTDEV(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153945				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149934				0	gl	To find the standard deviation of the weight for all children of the same age in the example (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150630				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DSTDEV(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153536				0	gl	In row 14, under Age, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>7, 8, 9,\</item\> and so on, one after the other. The result shown is the standard deviation of the weight of all children of this age.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150429				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>DSTDEVP function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>standard deviations in databases;based on populations\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150429				0	gl	BDDESVESTP				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145598				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBSTDABWN\"\>DSTDEVP calculates the standard deviation of a population based on all cells of a data range which match the search criteria.\</ahelp\> The records from the example are treated as the whole population.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145307				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	gl	DSTDEVP(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153322				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155431				0	gl	To find the standard deviation of the weight for all children of the same age at Joe's birthday party (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148411				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DSTDEVP(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	gl	In row 14, under Age, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>7, 8, 9,\</item\> and so on, one after the other. The result is the standard deviation of the weight for all same-aged children whose weight was checked.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154794				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>DSUM function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>calculating;sums in Calc databases\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>sums;cells in Calc databases\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154794				0	gl	BDSUMA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149591				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBSUMME\"\>DSUM returns the total of all cells in a database field in all rows (records) that match the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146128				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150989				0	gl	DSUM(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159079				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152766				0	gl	To find the length of the combined distance to school of all children at Joe's birthday party (scroll up, please) who are in second grade, enter the following formula in B16:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151312				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DSUM(A1:E10;"Distance to School";A13:E14)\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150596				0	gl	Enter \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\> in row 14 under Grade. The sum (1950) of the distances to school of all the children who are in second grade is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155614				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>DVAR function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>variances;based on samples\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155614				0	gl	BDVAR				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154418				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBVARIANZ\"\>DVAR returns the variance of all cells of a database field in all records that match the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\> The records from the example are treated as a sample of data. A representative result cannot be obtained from a sample population of less than one thousand.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154825				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156138				0	gl	DVAR(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151257				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153701				0	gl	To find the variance of the weight of all children of the same age of the above example (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153676				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DVAR(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153798				0	gl	In row 14, under Age, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>7, 8, 9,\</item\> and so on, one after the other. You will see as a result the variance of the weight values for all children of this age.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153880				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>DVARP function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>variances;based on populations\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153880				0	gl	BDVARP				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155119				0	gl	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBVARIANZEN\"\>DVARP calculates the variance of all cell values in a database field in all records that match the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\> The records are from the example are treated as an entire population.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145774				0	gl	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153776				0	gl	DVARP(Database; DatabaseField; SearchCriteria)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151110				0	gl	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147099				0	gl	To find the variance of the weight for all children of the same age at Joe's birthday party (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147322				0	gl	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DVARP(A1:E10;"Weight";A13:E14)\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146902				0	gl	In row 14, under Age, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>7, 8, 9,\</item\> and so on, one after the other. The variance of the weight values for all children of this age attending Joe's birthday party appears.				20200411 15:09:53
