helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id5338602				0	gl	The "Plain" type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5342265				0	gl	If you select the "Plain" type of rules, an empty paragraph is inserted at the position of the cursor. This paragraph has the style "Horizontal Line", with a line as the lower border of the paragraph. You can edit that Paragraph Style to change the properties of all "Plain" rules in your document. For example you can set the left indent to 3 inches, or you can change the line style, thickness, and color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id707113				0	gl	To edit the "Plain" rule style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5267494				0	gl	Escolla \<emph\>Formato - Estilos e formatado\</emph\> para abrir a xanela \<emph\>Estilos e formatado\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5074922				0	gl	In the listbox at the bottom, select to display "All Styles".				20200411 15:09:53
