helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130004.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	Estilo de numeración				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155961				0	gl	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130004.xhp\" name=\"Numbering Style\"\>Numbering Style\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149501				0	gl	Here you can create a Numbering Style. The Numbering Styles are organized in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05130004.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	gl	When a Numbering Style is created, a name is assigned to the numbering. This is why such templates are also called "named" numberings. Unnamed numberings, which are used for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#formatierung\" name=\"direct formatting\"\>direct formatting\</link\>, can be created in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Numbering/bullets\"\>Bullets and Numbering\</link\> dialog or with the icons of the \<link href=\"text/swriter/main0206.xhp\" name=\"object bar\"\>object bar\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gl	Etiquetas especiais				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154106				0	gl	\<bookmark_value\>tags; in $[officename] Writer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] Writer; special HTML tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML;special tags for fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields;HTML import and export\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>time fields;HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date fields;HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DocInformation fields\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154106				0	gl	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090007.xhp\" name=\"Special Tags\"\>Special Tags\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153669				0	gl	Cando se garda un documento con campos como HTML, $[officename] converte automaticamente os campos Data, Hora e Información do documento en etiquetas HTML especiais. O contido dos campos insírese entre as etiquetas HTML de abertura e pechamento dos campos convertidos. Estas etiquetas non se corresponden coas HTML estándar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960				0	gl	Nos documentos HTML, os campos de $[officename] Writer están identificados coa etiqueta <SDFIELD>. O tipo de campo, o formato e o nome do campo especial inclúense na etiqueta HTML de abertura. O formato dunha etiqueta de campo recoñecida por un filtro HTML depende do tipo de campo.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154570				0	gl	Campos de data e hora				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149696				0	gl	Nos campos "Data" e "Hora", o parámetro TYPE equivale a DATETIME. O formato da data ou da hora especifícase mediante o parámetro SDNUM; por exemplo, DD:MM:AA para as datas ou HH:MM:SS para a hora.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155183				0	gl	Nos campos de data e hora fixa, a data ou hora especifícase mediante o parámetro SDVAL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485				0	gl	A táboa seguinte mostra exemplos de etiquetas HTML especiais de data e hora que $[officename] recoñece como campos:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3151257				0	gl	Campos				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970				0	gl	Etiqueta $[officename] 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147102				0	gl	A Data é fixa				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153634				0	gl	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDVAL="35843,4239988426" SDNUM="1031;1031;DD/MM/AA">17/02/98</SDFIELD>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155137				0	gl	A Data é variábel				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275				0	gl	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDNUM="1031;1031;DD/MM/AA">17/02/98</SDFIELD>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3145774				0	gl	A Hora é fixa				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155915				0	gl	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDVAL="35843,4240335648" SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS">10:10:36</SDFIELD>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3150110				0	gl	A Hora é variábel				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862				0	gl	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS">10:10:36</SDFIELD>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147409				0	gl	Campos Información do documento				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147487				0	gl	No caso dos campos Información do documento, o parámetro TYPE equivale a DOCINFO. O parámetro SUBTYPE mostra o tipo de campo específico, por exemplo, do campo "Creado", SUBTYPE=CREATE. Nos campos Información do documento de data e hora, o parámetro FORMAT equivale a DATE ou TIME, e o parámetro SDNUM indica o formato de número utilizado. O parámetro SDFIXED indica se o contido do campo é fixo ou non.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147501				0	gl	O contido dun campo fixo de data ou hora equivale ao parámetro SDVAL ou entón ao texto existente entre as etiquetas HTML SDFIELD.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	gl	A táboa seguinte mostra exemplos de etiquetas HTML especiais dos campos Información do documento que $[officename] recoñece como campos:				20200411 15:09:53
